Correct ECS flow
Root user → IAM → Roles
Technically, you should not use the root user for normal AWS work.
Create/manage the IAM role using an IAM admin/user with appropriate permissions.
Create IAM Role
Trusted entity: AWS service
Use case: Elastic Container Service (ECS)
Choose ECS Task / Task execution role depending on what you're creating.
Attach the required permissions.
Give the role a name.
Switch to your normal IAM user
Open ECS (Elastic Container Service).
Create Task Definition
ECS → Task Definitions → Create.
Choose launch type/compute options as required.
Configure:
CPU
Memory
Container
Docker image URI
Port mappings, if your app needs them
Select:
Task role
Task execution role
Create the ECS Cluster
ECS → Clusters → Create cluster.
The cluster is basically the logical place where your ECS services/tasks run.
Create a Service inside the cluster
Select your Task Definition.
Specify how many tasks you want running.
Configure networking, load balancer, etc., if required.
ECS deploys/runs the task
The service launches tasks based on your task definition.
